{"timestamp":"2026-09-28T17:16:50.215Z","ordinal":18,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a0e904-f0a7-71e3-a0b5-85cd731ce688","call_id":"call_X9XFq3AMHEYz3qVZHKO6PMuE","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"fb8ea7\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.004405394,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":12081,\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 12081)\\nTotal output lines: 487\\n\\n.\\n..\\n.ssh\\n.tmp-tiered-serve-container.tar1355138299\\n.vast\\nbin\\nclean_up_GH.sh\\nexperiment-results\\nexport_container.sh\\ngithub-ssh\\nlaunch.sh\\nmodel_map.sh\\npatches\\nrun_experiment_tmux.sh\\nsetup_reboot.sh\\nstartup-patches\\ntiered-serve-container.tar\\n# CD3 Hybrid Crash Analysis\\n\\n## Conclusion\\n\\nThe immediate failure is a CPU write beyond a writable CUDA-driver internal\\nbuffer while processing the K batch in `HybridKVPlan::submit`. This is not\\nthe client connection error, and the evidence does not show an OOM kill.\\nThe user confirmed that CSR completed under the same request rate, prompt\\ncount, and Nsight conditions. The leading investigation target is therefore\\nthe CD3 hybrid/segment transition: transfer construction, segment reuse, and\\npipeline synchronization. A fault inside libcuda does not establish that the\\ndriver is the originating defect. Isolated valid copies did not reproduce\\nthe crash; application memory corruption or a workload-dependent interaction\\nwith the driver/profiler remain possible.\\n\\nProduction source, experiment settings, and installed libraries were not\\nchanged during this diagnosis. No serving experiment was restarted.\\n\\n## Original Failure\\n\\n- Container: `tiered-serve`; repo: `/root/projects/tiered-serve`\\n- Suite: `benchmark_results/serving_nsys/20260928T144024Z`\\n- Cell: `r01-cd3-kvcomp-c8192-q1p4-g16-hybrid`\\n- Core (preserved before the authorized serial diagnostic):\\n  `/root/cd3-serial-diagnostic-backup/original-pipeline.core`; process/LWP 13469\\n- Matching original native extension is preserved under\\n  `/root/cd3-serial-diagnostic-backup/native/`.\\n- Signal: SIGSEGV, `si_code=2` (access protection violation)\\n- Last logged scheduler step: 4462\\n- Capture had completed at forward 1907, triggered by offered request 600.\\n- User-mode CUDA driver: `/usr/local/cuda-13.2/compat/libcuda.so.1`\\n- Compatibility package: `cuda-compat-13-2 595.45.04-1ubuntu1`\\n- Kernel driver: 580.105.08\\n\\nThe native stack is:\\n\\n```\\nHybridKVPlan::submit\\ncudaMemcpyBatchAsync\\ncuMemcpyBatchAsync_v2\\nlibcuda.so.1 internal functions\\n```\\n\\n## Exact Fault\\n\\nGDB stopped at PC `0x0000ee07e8b11bbc`:\\n\\n```\\nstr wzr, [x6, x0, lsl #2]\\nx6 = 0x200bfd0d8\\nx0 = 5345\\nfault address = 0x200c0245c\\n```\\n\\nELF core program headers identify:\\n\\n| Range | Permissions |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| `0x200800000..0x200c00000` | Read/write |\\n| `0x200c00000..0x201200000` | No access |\\n\\nThere are 12,072 bytes left from `x6` to the writable boundary. The driver is\\npreparing to embed 21,384 bytes and first zeroes the final 4-byte word. That\\nwrite is 9,308 bytes beyond the writable boundary. The next instructions\\nwould call `memcpy` from the host source into this same internal buffer.\\n\\nThe driver source register is `0xedbbfb66b800`, exactly matching zero-based\\ndescriptor 124 in the original K batch:\\n\\n```\\nsource      0xedbbfb66b800\\ndestination 0x433b635030\\nsize        21384\\n```\\n\\nThe fault address is neither this source nor this destination. The source lies\\ninside the registered hugepage mapping `hp_tensor_kv_3`.\\n\\n## Checks Against the Core and Source\\n\\n- K batch: 142 descriptors, 40,356,064 bytes; V batch: 140 descriptors,\\n  40,250,552 bytes. All three vector lengths match on each side; capacity is\\n  29,134 entries. No null/negative-sized descriptor was found.\\n- Every source interval is within a readable core mapping. This does not by\\n  itself prove CUDA registration/lifetime, so ownership was checked separately.\\n- Destination intervals do not overlap within either batch.\\n- The plan represents 1,723 storage rows and binds ring 0. Its storage remains\\n  owned, has readers acquired, and is not marked poisoned.\\n- All 107 retained segment leases have matching generations, are allocated,\\n  and have positive reader counts. No released-segment evidence was found.\\n- The failed descriptor starts at offset 0 in segment 15639, generation 11.\\n  Its length and the segment's used length both equal 21,384 bytes, within\\n  the 65,536-byte capacity. At the crash it has 29 record references and one\\n  reader. This snapshot cannot exclude an earlier lifecycle error.\\n- All 54 K and 53 V exception-copy spans fit inside leased segments. Their\\n  respective byte sums and contiguous destination extents equal 1,292,208\\n  and 1,200,480 bytes, matching the plan's declared entry-word totals.\\n- Submission holds the native plan mutex. Sources are retained through the\\n  H2D completion event; the failed plan had not finished its first submission.\\n- Source uses one attribute with `srcAccessOrder=Stream`, attribute index 0,\\n  and the CUDA 13 eight-argument signature. Build headers and loaded runtime\\n  are CUDA 13.2; the CUDA 12/13 argument-count mismatch does not match this case.\\n- The cgroup reported `oom=0`, `oom_kill=0`; no corresponding kernel OOM/Xid\\n  message was found at the failure time.\\n\\nCUDA's API contract permits the one-attribute index arrangement and requires\\nsource lifetime through stream consumption:\\nhttps://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/archive/13.2.1/cuda-driver-api/group__CUDA__MEM.html\\n\\n## Diagnostic Runs and Limits\\n\\nA standalone C++ CUDA test used the original K descriptor sizes and, after\\nthe initial aligned test, the original source/destination offsets modulo\\n64 KiB. Each allocation remained live through stream synchronization. All\\n10,000-iteration cases below passed with a final copied-data check:\\n\\n1. CUDA-pinned host allocation, aligned addresses.\\n2. CUDA-pinned host allocation, original address alignment.\\n3. Registered anonymous host mapping.\\n4. Registered mapping with Nsight 2026.2.1 injection, profiler start/stop,\\n   and the original precapture mode; copies continue after capture stops.\\n5. Registered 16 GiB hugepage, bound to NUMA node 0.\\n6. Registered hugepage with GPU virtual memory backed by 2 MiB allocations,\\n   approximating the expandable-segment allocator used by the workload.\\n\\nThese are focused diagnostics, not reproductions of the full serving state.\\nThey do not establish that the original bug is fixed or that a driver update,\\ndisabling nsys, or replacing batched copies would fix it. They omit the original\\nsequence of changing batches, model kernels, concurrent encoders, and long-lived\\nallocator/profiler state. Final resource check: GPU 36 MiB / 0%, 23 hugepages free.\\n\\n## Remaining Discriminating Work\\n\\nBoth current CSR and hybrid use `cudaMemcpyBatchAsync` with the same source\\naccess-order attributes. CSR transfers each side's exception arena as one\\ncontiguous copy, combines K/V H2D submission, and decodes the pair after H2D.\\nHybrid gathers many segment spans, submits K/V separately, and uses separate\\nK/V completion events. These changed behaviors must be separated: segment\\nstorage with serialized transfer/decode, segment storage with alternate copy\\nsubmission, and lifecycle checks spanning repeated retire/reuse cycles. Such\\ndiagnostic variants are not validated production fixes.\\n\\nBefore another full serving run, preserve the original core because the next\\ncrash can overwrite `core`. A controlled rerun of the failing cell needs native\\nbatch-call records immediately before submission (copy arguments and source\\nownership), plus an A/B without Nsight and, separately, without the custom\\n`stack_pool.so` memory interposer. The interposer's global free-list is not\\nthread-safe and ignores mapping ownership/protection when pooling; this is a\\nseparate risk, not evidence that it caused this particular fault.\\n\\nIf the same internal overflow reproduces with independently valid inputs,\\nisolate the sequence into a standalone case before claiming a confirmed NVIDIA\\ndriver defect. Driver or transfer-path changes should be evaluated separately\\nbecause they can change the timing and overlap being measured.\\n\\n## Evidence Files\\n\\n- Host GDB output: `/tmp/cd3-core-inspection.txt`, `/tmp/cd3-driver-inspection.txt`\\n- Host diagnostic source: `/tmp/tieredserve_nsys_patch/batch_repro.cpp`\\n- Container extracted descriptors: `/tmp/cd3-crash-batch-0.json`,\\n  `/tmp/cd3-crash-batch-1.json`\\n- Container diagnostic binary/source: `/tmp/cd3-batch-repro`,\\n  `/tmp/cd3-batch-repro.cpp`\\n- Container diagnostic Nsight report: `/tmp/cd3-diagnostic-profile.nsys-rep`\\n\\nThe diagnostic report is separate from the actual experiment reports.\\n/home/ubuntu/whchoi/experiment-results/cd3-kv4-20260916/tests-kv4.log\\n/home/ubuntu/whchoi/experiment-results/cd3-kv4-20260916/tests-kv3.log\\n/home/ubuntu/whchoi/experiment-results/cd3-kv4-20260916/tests-before-change.log\\n/home/ubuntu/whchoi/experiment-results/cd3-kv4-20260916/serving.log\\n/home/ubuntu/whchoi/experiment-results/cd3-20260827/cao_p4_fused_actual_b64.log\\n/home/ubuntu/whchoi/experiment-results/cd3-20260827/cao_cd3_fused_actual_b64.log\\n/home/ubuntu/whchoi/experiment-results/cd3-20260827/cao_cd3_dense_actual_b64.log\\n/home/ubuntu/whchoi/experiment-results/pinned-allocator-fix-20260916/serving.log\\n/home/ubuntu/whchoi/experiment-results/cd3-kv-20260916-cpu-improvements/verification.log\\n/home/ubuntu/whchoi/experiment-results/cd3-20260901-route/qkv_all80_r0.log\\n/home/ubuntu/whchoi/experiment-results/cd3-20260901-route/prefill_raw_forced.log\\n/home/ubuntu/whchoi/experiment-results/cd3-20260901-route/prefill